# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env — it is gitignored, and `docs/05-stack.md`
# explains why that rule is verified with `git check-ignore -v` rather than trusted.
#
# On the district's server this file IS the secret store, deliberately (ADR-0007, ADR-0011):
# one machine in the DC office, operable by one person at 02:00. A secrets manager would add
# a network dependency, an account and a renewal nobody is watching, to protect a file that
# sits on the same disk as the database it unlocks. What the file needs instead:
#
#   chown dnc:dnc app/.env && chmod 600 app/.env
#
# `src/config.ts` checks all of this at boot and says what is missing in one log line, rather
# than letting a mistake surface at 02:00 inside the backup job. Anything that would only make
# the district *less protected* warns and keeps running — a process that will not start is a
# district that cannot report an emergency (INV-01).

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_ENV=development

# The record itself. The process refuses to start without this, and refuses to start in
# production if it is still the line below.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/dnc_dev

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PORT=3000

# error | warn | info | debug
LOG_LEVEL=info

# How often the escalation and notification passes run. Default 15000.
# ESCALATION_INTERVAL_MS=15000

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups (ADR-0011)
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where nightly dumps are written. Defaults to app/var/backups.
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/lib/dnc/backups

# Needed only when `pg_dump` on PATH is the wrong version. On Debian /usr/bin/pg_dump is
# `pg_wrapper`, which picked 16 against a 17 server — see the CI workflow.
# PG_BIN=/usr/lib/postgresql/17/bin

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Off-site backup — SECRETS. Waiting on the district (R-06).
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# All three are needed together. With none of them set, nightly dumps still run and stay on
# this machine; `/health` and Administration → Backups both say plainly that no copy has ever
# left the district. With a bucket but no passphrase, the upload refuses every night rather
# than sending the district's record out unencrypted — that is deliberate, and the boot check
# warns about it so nobody discovers it after a fire.
#
# The passphrase must be at least 16 characters and is what a restore will need. If it is
# lost, every off-site copy is unreadable. Keep it somewhere that is not this machine.

# GCS_BUCKET=
# GCS_TOKEN=
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weather (R-16)
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Defaults to Bannu city's published coordinates — a default, not a finding. The district may
# want the reading taken at the DC office, or at a tehsil that floods first.

# WEATHER_LAT=32.9889
# WEATHER_LON=70.6056

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests only
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The integration suite refuses to run against a fake and says so loudly if this is missing.
# Under CI a missing value is a hard failure, never a skip — otherwise one broken secret drops
# every integration test and the build goes green having run a fraction of them.

# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5433/dnc_test
